From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReaperOfVeriod <oeps46@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:00:46 +0000
Subject: big modded levels

Let a modded level use more than 32 MiB.

- load_level_gameplay (FUN_L00_00241940): with OPENRAC_HAS_DISC (the port), the level heap
  checks (CHECK_LEVEL_HEAP) and the expanded arena's own file-order moby map
  (EXPANDED_LEVEL_RAM, true only above 32 MiB of guest RAM, a modded level's); without it
  EXPANDED_LEVEL_RAM is 0 and CHECK_LEVEL_HEAP nothing. The port can give a modded level more
  than the console's 32 MiB; the retail code has no such path. The PS2 build compiles the added
  branch away: Lombyte f809a274's check-unit.py FUN_L00_00241940 gives EXACT (PAL's
  level_gameplay_loading.c with the same change: overlay_file_check.py, 0 problems).
